      "content": "that's an interesting way to look at it. but looking closer at the demographics, Zone A is almost entirely white and Zone B has a very high percentage of minority residents and immigrants. aren't you basically saying that we should prioritize white, wealthy communities because they're \"safer\" investments, while basically leaving the minority communities to wait for whatever is left over? isn't that just reinforcing the systemic inequality that makes these areas vulnerable in the first place?",
